================================================================================
Provenance
================================================================================

The numerical core of meteor-cfd is implemented from published literature.
Every formulation is specified and cited in `rust/SPEC-LIT.md`, and every
source file carries a header naming the papers it was written from and the
line "No GPL-licensed source was consulted." All 191 source files under
`rust/` (`src/`, `cuda/`, `tests/`, `build.rs`) carry both that line and the
copyright header, and every one of them is classified in `rust/PROVENANCE.md`
— checked in both directions.

That is not a claim you have to take on trust. It is a test:

    cd rust && cargo test --release --lib provenance_audit

`provenance_audit::every_source_file_declares_its_provenance` walks the four
roots named above and fails naming any file that is missing either line;
`provenance_audit::notice_and_provenance_quote_the_real_file_count` reads the
count back out of this file and out of `rust/PROVENANCE.md`, so adding a
source file without updating them fails in CI rather than in an audit. The
count was wrong once — 85 of 105 files carried the line while both documents
said 105 — which is why it is checked mechanically now.

meteor-cfd reads and writes the OpenFOAM ASCII case format so that existing
pre- and post-processing tools can be used with it. A file format is not a work
of authorship: the reader and writer here were written from the format as it
appears in data files. meteor-cfd links against no part of OpenFOAM, contains
no OpenFOAM source, and is neither derived from nor affiliated with OpenFOAM,
the OpenFOAM Foundation, or OpenCFD Ltd.

`rust/PROVENANCE.md` is the per-file record. `LICENSING.md` records what was
removed from this repository's history, and why.

